{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "CalKit - Public Holidays, Business Days & Timezone API (150+ countries)",
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "# CalKit: Public Holidays, Business Days and Time Zone API\n\nPublic holidays for 250+ country and territory codes with regional subdivisions, business-day maths that skips weekends and holidays, and time-zone lookup and conversion. Built for deadlines, delivery dates and scheduling across borders.\n\n**Who it's for:** e-commerce and logistics, payroll and HR, fintech, booking and scheduling apps, and SaaS products with SLAs.\n\n## Use cases\n- Show accurate 'arrives by' dates that skip bank holidays.\n- Calculate invoice due dates and SLA deadlines in business days.\n- Block bookings or payouts on public holidays in a customer's region.\n- Find a user's time zone from GPS coordinates.\n- Convert meeting times between offices, with daylight saving handled.\n\n## Quickstart\nSubscribe on RapidAPI (a free plan is available), copy your key, then:\n\n```bash\ncurl --request GET \\\n  --url 'https://calkit-public-holidays-business-days-timezones.p.rapidapi.com/holidays?country=GB&subdiv=ENG&year=2026' \\\n  --header 'X-RapidAPI-Key: YOUR_RAPIDAPI_KEY' \\\n  --header 'X-RapidAPI-Host: calkit-public-holidays-business-days-timezones.p.rapidapi.com'\n```\n\n## Authentication\nEvery request goes through RapidAPI. Send `X-RapidAPI-Key` (your key) and `X-RapidAPI-Host` (`calkit-public-holidays-business-days-timezones.p.rapidapi.com`) on every call. Requests that bypass the gateway are rejected with `403`.\n\n## Good to know\n- Dates are ISO 8601 (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Supported years: 1950-2100 for holiday lists.\n- Use `weekend` for countries with non Saturday/Sunday weekends (e.g. `fri,sat`).\n- Holiday definitions follow official sources as encoded in the open-source holidays library; occasional one-off holidays may be added late.\n\n## Rate limits and plans\nRequest quotas and per-second limits depend on the RapidAPI plan you subscribe to; see the Pricing tab. When a limit is reached the gateway returns `429 Too Many Requests`; retry with exponential backoff or move to a higher plan.\n\n## Errors\nAll errors are JSON. The API returns `{\"error\": \"<reason>\"}` with a meaningful HTTP status: `404` not found, `422` missing or invalid parameter. Gateway errors (`401`/`403`/`429`) come from RapidAPI as `{\"message\": \"<reason>\"}`.\n\n## Data sources and licences\n- Holiday data: python-holidays library (MIT licence).\n- Time zone boundaries: tzfpy, built on timezone-boundary-builder data derived from OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0).\n- Time zone rules: IANA Time Zone Database (public domain).\n\n## MCP (AI agents)\nThis API is also available as a Model Context Protocol server at `POST /mcp` on the same RapidAPI host; see the MCP endpoint for setup.",
    "contact": {
      "name": "API support on RapidAPI",
      "url": "https://rapidapi.com/user/Olly-1VN9JTXKG"
    }
  },
